        usage: "USAGE:\n  bsc memory horizon <id> now|future [--dir <store>]",
    },
    CmdDoc {
        name: "kind",
        summary: "reclassify a memory - lesson | highlight | record | ambient | note",
        usage: "USAGE:\n  bsc memory kind <id> lesson|highlight|record|ambient|note [--dir <store>]\n\nThe promotion path off `note`, and off `ambient` once a captured thought turns out to be a real\nlesson or highlight. An unknown kind is refused, naming the ones that exist.",
    },
    CmdDoc {
        name: "brief",
        summary: "what a session touching these nodes should be told — the block written at launch",
        usage: "USAGE:\n  bsc memory brief <ref> [<ref>...] [--json] [--dir <store>]\n\nRenders the block a launching session receives: the lessons and highlights edged to the nodes it will\ntouch, the standing (unscoped) lessons, and the COUNT of record notes plus the command that reaches\nthem. `record` is pointed at rather than quoted; `ambient` and `note` never appear — an unpromoted\ncapture is noise and unclassified means unreviewed.\n\nZERO related memories still renders a block that SAYS zero: nothing-is-recorded and nobody-looked are\ndifferent facts, and an absent block says the second while meaning the first.",
    },
    CmdDoc { name: "done", summary: "mark a memory handled / folded elsewhere", usage: "USAGE:\n  bsc memory done <id> [--dir <store>]" },
